.TH DANBY-STRAINS 1
.SH NAME
danby-strains \- two epidemic strains sharing susceptible hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/strains
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Temple/strains
is an interactive live simulation of two epidemic strains sharing susceptible hosts.
It integrates the model continuously and redraws its state as parameters or
initial conditions change.
.SH MODEL
S'=-betaA S A-betaB S B; A'=betaA S A-gamma A; B'=betaB S B-gamma B.
.PP
The strains compete only through the shared susceptible pool and have a common recovery rate.
.SH DISPLAY
The traces show susceptible, strain A, and strain B. The strain with greater effective transmission usually depletes susceptible hosts first.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the view to change the initial strain mixture. Bottom tracks set both transmission rates and recovery.
.PP
Space pauses or resumes the simulation.  Period advances one displayed step
while paused.  The
.B r
key restores the default initial state and
.B q
or Escape exits.
.SH INTERPRETATION
The quantities are normalized unless physical units are stated explicitly.
The display is a visualization of a low-dimensional differential-equation
model, not an agent simulation or a prediction of a particular real system.
Parameter changes restart the displayed history so trajectories from different
settings are not joined.
.SH NUMERICS
The state is advanced by the general-purpose
.B Numerics
fourth-order Runge-Kutta solver.  Small negative values caused by numerical
roundoff are clamped for nonnegative population and stock models.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/strains.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR numerics (2)

